          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.086,
            0.412,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": "Complete the justification."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.122,
            0.846,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "？ Is an m × n grid tileable with 2 × 1 tiles, if both m and n are even? If yes, come up with a general strategy to tile it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.167,
            0.847,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "One general strategy for this case is to cover each column with vertical tiles. This is possible because the number of rows is even."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.213,
            0.692,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_22_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.439,
            0.847,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "? Is an $m \\times n$ grid tileable with 2 × 1 tiles, if one of m and n is even and the other is odd? If yes, come up with a general strategy to tile it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.494,
            0.847,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "？ Is an $m \\times n$ grid tileable with 2 × 1 tiles, if both m and n are odd? Give reasons."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.551,
            0.646,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "Here is a $5 \\times 3$ grid, with a unit square removed. Now, it has an even number of unit squares. Is it tileable with 2 × 1 tiles?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.72,
            0.597,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "Is the following region tileable with $2 \\times 1$ tiles?"
        },
